+# ---------------------------------------------------------------- arm64: the code out of the image
+# The game image (ELF, at window + 0x20000000) keeps its data there, where game code's 32-bit pointers reach it, but its
+# code runs from the executable: iOS runs only signed code, never code mapped at run time. Game code addresses its data
+# absolutely (-mcmodel=large, cc_unit.py) and the rest of its code relatively, so it runs anywhere, as long as it moves
+# whole and by whole pages. What it cannot have: code addressing data relatively, or holding a code address absolutely.
+# Data holding a code address (the constructor list, initialised function pointers) is corrected at startup by how far
+# the code moved: game_text_fixups.s lists where (host/macos.c).
